[2026-03-15T00:27:26.048Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NNJFHNcEQkvijfAPxNHNJL","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n\nThe tool provides exploratory and explanatory functions for investigating recordings:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** identify what happened and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection with execution hit counts\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Point details including variable values and stack frames\n- DOM element and React component inspection\n\n**Investigation Approach:**\n\nThe documentation recommends framing questions, using exploratory tools to find relevant events, applying explanatory tools to understand causation, forming hypotheses with supporting data, and explaining conclusions with evidence.\n\n**Notable Guidance:**\n\n\"The most important thing to remember when using Replay MCP to investigate a recording is to not jump to conclusions.\" The Logpoint tool is highlighted as particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution points.\n\nThe tool essentially treats recordings as searchable databases of execution points and DOM elements, enabling detailed post-hoc analysis of application behavior."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24c86dd7-4f1e-4262-a2f5-95ade9fc16a6","uuid":"2a4c875a-f6e7-4264-bd8f-f6b4f3d23df1","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Skill File Content\n\n**Name:** replay-mcp\n\n**Description:** Tool for inspecting https://replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution data.\n\n**Key Capabilities:**\n\nThe tool provides exploratory and explanatory functions for investigating recordings:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** identify what happened and when:\n- Error detection (uncaught exceptions, React errors)\n- Timeline analysis (console messages, network requests, React renders)\n- Source code inspection with execution hit counts\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events occurred:\n- Dependency tracking showing cause-and-effect relationships\n- Point details including variable values and stack frames\n- DOM element and React component inspection\n\n**Investigation Approach:**\n\nThe documentation recommends framing questions, using exploratory tools to find relevant events, applying explanatory tools to understand causation, forming hypotheses with supporting data, and explaining conclusions with evidence.\n\n**Notable Guidance:**\n\n\"The most important thing to remember when using Replay MCP to investigate a recording is to not jump to conclusions.\" The Logpoint tool is highlighted as particularly valuable for tracking expression values across execution points.\n\nThe tool essentially treats recordings as searchable databases of execution points and DOM elements, enabling detailed post-hoc analysis of application behavior.","durationMs":3434,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-15T00:27:26.484Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RYDK2g2Yi4yLJPDaDEcPp7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It enables installation, session recording, upload management, and authentication.\n\n## Key Installation Methods\nInstall globally via: `npm i -g replayio`, `yarn add -g replayio`, `pnpm i -g replayio`, or `bun i -g replayio`\n\n## Authentication Setup\nVisit https://app.replay.io settings to create an API key, then set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Primary Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `info` | Shows installed Replay dependencies and CLI version |\n| `list` | Displays all local recordings with metadata |\n| `login`/`logout` | Account authentication management |\n| `record [url]` | Launches Replay Browser to record a session |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Deletes one or more recordings |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Uploads recordings; returns viewable URL |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Uploads source maps for debugging |\n| `help` | Shows all available commands |\n\n## Standard Workflow\n1. Run `replayio record https://myapp.com` to start recording\n2. Close the browser when done\n3. Execute `replayio upload <recording-id>` if not auto-prompted\n4. Use the provided URL to access your recording\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using the `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"24c86dd7-4f1e-4262-a2f5-95ade9fc16a6","uuid":"ac403493-86f2-4204-a629-513e1516e669","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Skill Reference\n\n## Overview\nReplay CLI is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. It enables installation, session recording, upload management, and authentication.\n\n## Key Installation Methods\nInstall globally via: `npm i -g replayio`, `yarn add -g replayio`, `pnpm i -g replayio`, or `bun i -g replayio`\n\n## Authentication Setup\nVisit https://app.replay.io settings to create an API key, then set it as the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Primary Commands\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `info` | Shows installed Replay dependencies and CLI version |\n| `list` | Displays all local recordings with metadata |\n| `login`/`logout` | Account authentication management |\n| `record [url]` | Launches Replay Browser to record a session |\n| `remove [ids...]` | Deletes one or more recordings |\n| `upload [ids...]` | Uploads recordings; returns viewable URL |\n| `upload-source-maps` | Uploads source maps for debugging |\n| `help` | Shows all available commands |\n\n## Standard Workflow\n1. Run `replayio record https://myapp.com` to start recording\n2. Close the browser when done\n3. Execute `replayio upload <recording-id>` if not auto-prompted\n4. Use the provided URL to access your recording\n\n## MCP Integration\nInstall Replay MCP Server in Claude to debug recorded applications using the `REPLAY_API_KEY` for authorization.","durationMs":4354,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
